# Portfolio style

Before editing any public copy, read and follow [STYLE.md](../../STYLE.md).

Hard rules:

- No em dashes (`—`). Use a period, comma, colon, or parentheses.
- Homepage work cards: sharp stake in the title; method/outcome in the support line.
- Never put research-hour totals on homepage teasers; they read like total tenure.
- Glia is a venture-backed startup; say so when introducing it.
- Prefer concrete, human language over agency jargon.
- Match existing page structure; change words, not layout, unless asked.
